    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d35">

                <pb facs="0107" n="27" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg27"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Senhor Brasil.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-04-27"><hi rendition="#italic">April 27,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 22.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your recent interview with the
                    Assistant Secretary of State, I have the honor to say that the Secretaries of
                    the Treasury, War, and the Navy, and the governor of New York have <pb
                        facs="0108" n="28" xml:id="pg28"/> been advised of the expected arrival of
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">Benjamin Constant</hi> at New York, and requested to
                    direct the authorities there to extend the customary courtesies to the
                    vessel.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
